{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>She is more righteous than I.</b> She is righteous in her words; from me she is with child. And our Sages interpreted (Sotah 10b) that a bat kol went forth and said: \"From me and from Him the matter came forth\" — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 38:26). But the correct interpretation is that it is like \"righteous and better than him\" (I Kings 2:32), and \"He said to David, You are more righteous than I, for you have done me good while I have done you evil\" (I Samuel 24:17) — she is more righteous in her deeds than I, for she is the righteous one and I am the one who sinned against her by not giving her to Shelah my son. The reason is that Shelah is the yavam (levir), and if he does not wish to take his yevamah (levirate sister-in-law), his father is the redeemer next in line after him, as I explained above (Ramban on Genesis 38:8) regarding the law of yibbum (levirate marriage)." "<b>And he knew her again no more.</b> After he had established seed for his sons, he did not wish to be with her any more, even though it was in his desire, for she is not forbidden to him and she was his wife according to the law of yevamot (levirate widows). And this is the meaning of the one who says (Sotah 10b): \"he did not cease\" — for it is written here \"and he did not add (וְלֹא יָסַף),\" and it is written there (Deuteronomy 5:19) \"a great voice and it did not cease (וְלֹא יָסָף).\""], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {0 "The phrase ממני ומאתי in the bat kol drash plays on the same Hebrew words but splits the meaning: 'from me' (from Yehudah) and 'from Him' (from Hashem).", 1 "The Sages in Sotah 10b derive from the parallel use of ולא יסף in both verses that just as in Deuteronomy it means 'did not cease,' so here it means Yehudah did not cease — i.e., the plain sense is the opposite of the surface reading. Ramban explains that he refrained despite desire, not because she was forbidden."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:41:58.607027251Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}